  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "Does \"Energy Drain\" require a non-immune enemy hero in range for my team to be able to regain 1 spent Life counter?",
      "answer": "Yes, you need to be able to target a hero first.\n\"If able\" after a comma makes the preceding step non-mandatory (p. 17), so it only applies to the \"discard\" step of the instructions.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I play an action if only some of its instructions can be performed?",
      "answer": "You must follow the cards instructions step by step, starting from the top.\n• If you cannot perform the first instruction (e.g., there is no valid target in range, or you cannot make the required movement), you may not perform the action at all.\n• After the first instruction is successfully exectued, you continue resolving the rest of the instructions in order.\n• If you reach an instruction that is not optional and you cannot perform it, the action immediately fizzles — no further instructions are resolved. You place the card on your hero dashboard, and your turn ends.\n_See page 10 of the rulebook for additional reference._",
      "source": "goa2-faq (common)"
    }
  ],
  "lore": "Gydion the Archwizard is an odd blend of ancient wisdom and forgetfulness that could make a goldfish look like a meticulous archivist. Despite this, he has an uncanny knack for invoking the right spells at exactly the right moment.",
